WEBVTT

00:00.567 --> 00:09.424
kanashige ni saku hana ni kimi no omokage wo mita

00:00.567 --> 00:09.424
I saw your image in the flower that is blossoming sorrowfully

00:09.937 --> 00:18.509
daisuki na ame nanoni naze ka kyou wa tsumetakute

00:09.937 --> 00:18.509
I love rain, yet it felt frosty today

00:18.651 --> 00:37.226
kisetsu wa meguri mori wa somerare kaze wa kanadete omoi afurete

00:18.651 --> 00:37.226
The season changed, the forest was colored, the wind played a tune, memories overflowed

00:37.600 --> 00:46.786
tsuki no kakera wo atsumete yume wo kazari nemuru

00:37.600 --> 00:46.787
Gather the pieces of the moon, decorate the dream and sleep

00:47.020 --> 00:56.153
toki no suna chiribametemo ano koro e kaeranai

00:47.020 --> 00:56.154
Even if I sprinkle the sand of time, I cannot return to the past

00:56.313 --> 01:05.420
ikiru imi sageshiteiru dare mo mina tabibito

00:56.313 --> 01:05.420
Those searching for the meaning of life are all travellers

01:05.769 --> 01:14.817
haruka naru tabiji tadori boku wa ima arukidasu

01:05.776 --> 01:14.817
I set my course on this endless journey

01:14.837 --> 01:22.812
ibara no michi no mukou e...

01:14.837 --> 01:22.812
for the place beyond the thorny path...

01:25.812 --> 01:30.732
The artist of life who produces miracles
with his godlike scalpel skills.

01:31.651 --> 01:33.986
The surgeon whom the era has yearned for.

01:34.862 --> 01:35.905
Black Jack.

01:58.568 --> 02:00.402
Your tongue is pale.

02:00.403 --> 02:01.742
Does food not taste good to you?

02:01.742 --> 02:03.613
You must be a picky eater then.

02:08.953 --> 02:11.747
Oh! Huh?! Yucky!

02:13.750 --> 02:15.834
What are you doing, Gonta?!

02:15.835 --> 02:16.835
Me?

02:16.836 --> 02:17.961
Didn't you do it?!

02:18.713 --> 02:21.653
Gonta, I'll move you to the back of the line!

02:21.883 --> 02:23.550
Um, Doctor,

02:24.052 --> 02:27.262
you aren't as pretty when you're mad.

02:27.263 --> 02:28.513
Yeah, yeah!

02:28.514 --> 02:29.473
Shush!

02:29.891 --> 02:32.684
Hey! Don't run!

02:34.896 --> 02:37.680
Dr. Shimizu, you have a guest from the mainland.

02:38.483 --> 02:39.249
From the mainland?

02:40.985 --> 02:41.888
Who is it?

02:44.146 --> 02:47.239
Originally by Tezuka Osamu "Pouring Rain"

02:44.146 --> 02:47.239
Pouring Rain, then Love

02:56.501 --> 02:57.391
Um...

03:03.549 --> 03:06.093
Are you Shimizu Ikuo-san's sister?

03:06.094 --> 03:09.513
Yes, but my brother died.

03:09.514 --> 03:11.191
I just heard the news.

03:11.557 --> 03:13.895
This was where he was buried under a mudslide?

03:14.268 --> 03:15.245
I'm sorry to hear that.

03:16.187 --> 03:18.255
He was the school doctor here.

03:18.747 --> 03:23.167
He was trying to rescue a kid right here when
he became a victim of the disaster.

03:23.402 --> 03:24.935
It was about a year ago.

03:25.238 --> 03:27.906
So, how did you know my brother?

03:36.666 --> 03:39.318
My tools were stolen when I was
on an official visit overseas.

03:39.585 --> 03:41.913
I was devastated that I couldn't operate on a patient.

03:43.339 --> 03:47.488
The man who gave me the scalpel that
saved that man's life was Dr. Shimizu.

03:48.985 --> 03:54.184
Because of that scalpel, I was able
to save a man's precious life.

03:54.945 --> 03:57.531
The Shimizu Family Sleeps Here

03:56.602 --> 03:58.962
This is to thank him for that time.

04:01.357 --> 04:02.357
A scalpel?

04:02.984 --> 04:04.542
This isn't an ordinary scalpel.

04:04.986 --> 04:06.346
It's very dear to me.

04:06.696 --> 04:10.574
I even spent a lot of money by asking
a well-known smith to sharpen it.

04:10.575 --> 04:11.867
It's a very special scalpel.

04:13.286 --> 04:16.705
I wanted Dr. Shimizu to try it.

04:21.168 --> 04:23.571
I'm sure he'd appreciate your intentions.

04:24.463 --> 04:26.339
Besides, my brother is gone now.

04:27.300 --> 04:29.459
Then you can use it.

04:30.094 --> 04:31.636
You're a doctor too, correct?

04:31.971 --> 04:36.050
Thank you, but I practice internal
medicine, so I don't use scalpels.

04:36.559 --> 04:38.518
But it should come in useful someday.

04:40.146 --> 04:42.105
I will not ever perform surgery.

04:42.398 --> 04:43.436
Please take it back.

04:43.608 --> 04:45.150
Isn't it dear to you?

04:52.074 --> 04:57.787
My brother handled both the duties
at the school and the village clinic.

04:59.123 --> 05:01.750
I came here to help my brother.

05:02.167 --> 05:06.296
But now I handle both of them.

05:06.297 --> 05:08.340
Bye, Doctor!

05:08.341 --> 05:09.107
Goodbye.

05:11.302 --> 05:13.011
When does the next ferry leave?

05:13.596 --> 05:14.678
The next ferry?

05:15.014 --> 05:15.930
I think...

05:23.856 --> 05:26.085
Doc, you're late.

05:26.359 --> 05:28.805
You said you'd be right back!

05:29.070 --> 05:30.028
Missy.

05:31.645 --> 05:33.740
What are you waiting for, Missy?

05:33.741 --> 05:36.493
The ferry won't be coming tonight, because of the storm.

05:36.494 --> 05:38.703
Ohmigewdness!

05:39.038 --> 05:40.455
Oh, Doc?

05:40.456 --> 05:43.690
If there isn't a ferry, use an airplane!

05:45.336 --> 05:46.836
There are no airplanes?

05:46.837 --> 05:47.962
Then I will...

05:48.506 --> 05:50.173
Hello?

05:55.971 --> 05:57.722
Isn't it a small island?

05:57.723 --> 05:59.298
Just like my home.

05:59.600 --> 06:03.690
So, did you consider working for a clinic in a bigger town?

06:06.617 --> 06:10.777
I loved my brother,

06:11.737 --> 06:13.610
so I wanted to help him.

06:14.897 --> 06:18.025
But you've remained on this island even after his death.

06:18.285 --> 06:21.632
Well, I have nowhere else to go.

06:22.219 --> 06:24.700
So it grew on you?

06:25.209 --> 06:26.042
Yes.

06:27.253 --> 06:30.880
It really is too bad that Dr. Shimizu is gone.

06:32.216 --> 06:35.778
We promised to have a drink together
when we met the next time.

06:36.011 --> 06:38.740
Yes, he was a skilled doctor.

06:42.119 --> 06:45.402
By the way, I haven't asked you for your name yet.

06:45.771 --> 06:47.841
I am Shimizu Kiyomi.

06:50.317 --> 06:51.793
I'm Black Jack.

07:01.704 --> 07:03.391
Dr. Shimizu!

07:04.757 --> 07:09.431
Our little Masashi just vomited
and is rolling around in pain!

07:09.951 --> 07:11.346
Is it food poisoning?

07:11.347 --> 07:12.180
I'll be right over.

07:13.015 --> 07:14.403
Dr. Shimizu!

07:15.560 --> 07:20.063
Right after my kid told me his head
hurt, he started vomiting!

07:20.064 --> 07:21.439
Yours too?

07:21.440 --> 07:22.118
Does he have a fever?

07:22.358 --> 07:24.276
Doctor, my Ayako is...

07:24.277 --> 07:26.611
Doctor, both my wife and kid are vomiting!

07:26.612 --> 07:27.538
They won't stop!

07:28.099 --> 07:30.365
1 must be food poisoning.

07:31.075 --> 07:32.576
Dr. Black Jack.

07:33.476 --> 07:34.494
Doctor,

07:36.706 --> 07:39.419
I'm sorry, but it looks like there is a
mass outbreak of food poisoning.

07:39.915 --> 07:41.751
Would you please help me?

07:42.534 --> 07:44.556
A mass outbreak of food poisoning?

07:44.714 --> 07:47.661
Yes. I must go tend to twenty or thirty people.

07:48.009 --> 07:49.718
Would you help me?

07:50.136 --> 07:52.351
Food poisoning is handled by internists.

07:52.680 --> 07:53.930
I'm a surgeon.

07:54.294 --> 07:57.058
But Doctor, it's an emergency!

07:57.421 --> 08:00.477
This isn't the time to argue about one's specialty!

08:01.939 --> 08:05.318
Anyway, I shouldn't be involved in it.

08:07.669 --> 08:10.735
Doctor, aren't you going to help me?

08:12.033 --> 08:14.367
My job is to flash scalpels around.

08:14.368 --> 08:15.712
And yours is internal medicine.

08:15.953 --> 08:18.744
You said so yourself.

08:19.332 --> 08:21.195
Fine, then!

08:22.460 --> 08:23.982
Let's go.

08:24.253 --> 08:25.704
I'll visit them all by myself.

08:29.967 --> 08:33.428
<i>I can't believe his attitude!</i>

08:36.015 --> 08:40.935
All the kids who bought and ate the food
that came on the last ferry must be getting sick.

08:41.303 --> 08:43.246
Doctor, what should we do?

08:43.481 --> 08:45.732
Keep him rested and also make sure he's warm.

08:46.817 --> 08:50.028
If his diarrhea persists, give him some
warm water or tea to drink.

08:51.072 --> 08:52.310
You feel dizzy?

08:53.032 --> 08:55.089
Then let's try this.

08:56.160 --> 08:57.994
Please come to the clinic if his condition worsens.

09:00.081 --> 09:02.663
<i>I'm really understaffed.</i>

09:03.209 --> 09:04.876
<i>But he is so...</i>

09:06.587 --> 09:07.879
Oh, Mr. Principal.

09:08.214 --> 09:10.051
Oh, Dr. Shimizu.

09:10.257 --> 09:11.779
What a disaster this is!

09:12.093 --> 09:14.344
And you're the only doctor around.

09:14.541 --> 09:16.721
Actually, there is one more,

09:16.722 --> 09:18.428
but he's useless.

09:19.600 --> 09:22.581
There are more patients over there, so excuse me.

09:23.676 --> 09:25.183
Thank you!

09:26.692 --> 09:30.068
I won't play tricks anymore.

09:30.069 --> 09:33.029
Gonta, show me your usual energy.

09:33.030 --> 09:34.489
You'll get well soon.

09:35.074 --> 09:36.430
Come on, Gonta.

09:41.914 --> 09:44.249
The school principal fell off a cliff.

09:44.250 --> 09:45.291
He's been seriously injured.

09:45.503 --> 09:46.417
When?!

09:46.418 --> 09:48.179
I just passed him on my bicycle.

09:49.004 --> 09:51.714
Looks like a strong gust hit his bicycle.

09:52.633 --> 09:54.317
He has serious internal bleeding,

09:54.635 --> 09:57.035
and there's a chance some of his
internal organs have ruptured.

09:57.471 --> 09:59.860
There were strong winds tonight on
top of the epidemic in the town.

10:00.266 --> 10:03.059
I thought there was a good chance
someone might be injured.

10:04.770 --> 10:09.524
You stayed at the clinic, just in case?

10:09.984 --> 10:10.856
That's right.

10:11.318 --> 10:15.841
The roads here are bad, and it's dark,
so I thought maybe I should stay here.

10:17.241 --> 10:18.752
Did the food poisoning affect their vision?

10:18.951 --> 10:20.660
Or did they have any problems speaking?

10:21.745 --> 10:24.747
No, there were no signs of nervous system abnormalities.

10:24.912 --> 10:26.855
Then it must be just regular food poisoning.

10:27.376 --> 10:29.168
Botulism would have been bad.

10:29.628 --> 10:31.671
Everyone should be fine after a couple days.

10:35.426 --> 10:37.594
Now, it's my turn.

10:42.850 --> 10:44.514
You should go get some rest.

10:44.852 --> 10:45.810
You have to work tomorrow.

10:47.021 --> 10:49.188
No, I'll help.

10:49.240 --> 10:50.961
This is a job for a surgeon.

10:51.191 --> 10:53.318
Then I'll help disinfect.

10:58.318 --> 11:00.062
<i>What amazing sharpness...</i>

11:00.409 --> 11:02.160
<i>So this is the scalpel?</i>

11:02.995 --> 11:05.398
As I thought, there is a tear in the ileum.

11:05.873 --> 11:07.707
A rock must have punctured it when he fell.

11:08.626 --> 11:10.047
<i>He's so dexterous.</i>

11:14.006 --> 11:16.841
<i>He's wonderful.</i>

11:30.989 --> 11:32.823
Looks like he's fine now.

11:34.534 --> 11:36.952
Is it true the principal was seriously injured?

11:36.953 --> 11:37.494
Yes.

11:38.121 --> 11:41.749
But a surgeon operated on him, so he's fine now.

11:42.500 --> 11:44.501
Did the replacement for your brother come?

11:45.424 --> 11:46.152
No,

11:46.671 --> 11:49.673
but he is better than my brother was.

11:55.764 --> 11:58.202
You've been stuck on this tiny island for so long.

11:58.475 --> 11:59.725
I'm sorry.

12:00.268 --> 12:01.644
It's OK.

12:02.354 --> 12:07.066
Since you have to wait, I'll fix you something good to eat.

12:07.067 --> 12:09.526
Then I would like some ochazuke.

12:07.067 --> 12:09.526
Ochazuke is a bowl of rice submerged in hot tea.

12:09.534 --> 12:10.754
Ochazuke?

12:11.247 --> 12:12.307
Do you like that?

12:12.534 --> 12:13.141
Yes.

12:14.491 --> 12:16.116
Then for tomorrow, would you like...

12:16.117 --> 12:17.076
Ochazuke.

12:18.954 --> 12:21.622
If there's no ferry until the day after tomorrow...

12:21.623 --> 12:22.665
Ochazuke.

12:24.584 --> 12:25.856
This is so mean.

12:26.127 --> 12:29.546
Would you try my real cooking at least once?

12:29.547 --> 12:30.313
Someday.

12:31.216 --> 12:32.558
Doctor!

12:32.676 --> 12:34.395
Dr. Kiyomi!

12:34.511 --> 12:37.538
Oh, Dr. Crazy Quilt, you're still around.

12:37.722 --> 12:40.182
Don't talk to him like that!

12:40.642 --> 12:46.230
The mayor is asking you to comment on
the completion of the new auditorium.

12:47.691 --> 12:49.572
Why do you have patches?

12:49.818 --> 12:51.443
Stop that!

12:51.444 --> 12:52.528
How rude!

12:56.700 --> 13:02.466
For a certain reason, someone else's
skin was transplanted onto me.

13:03.164 --> 13:05.055
Do you think all of my skin should be the same color?

13:05.344 --> 13:07.057
Definitely!

13:07.252 --> 13:11.026
Then it will look good when you marry
a beautiful woman like Dr. Kiyomi.

13:11.256 --> 13:13.715
Quit talking nonsense and go on home!

13:26.479 --> 13:28.730
The ferry isn't coming today again?

13:29.065 --> 13:31.358
A tropical storm?

13:31.359 --> 13:35.195
Does there happen to be a good-looking
female doctor there?

13:35.196 --> 13:38.471
And is she feeding you ochazuke?

13:39.064 --> 13:42.369
Remember, don't cheat on me!

13:41.506 --> 13:42.346
Cheat?

13:42.370 --> 13:43.857
I can tell!

13:46.166 --> 13:46.877
What?

13:46.947 --> 13:47.624
Nothing.

13:56.759 --> 14:09.438
I am proud to have an auditorium for this
small school as grand as the ones in Tokyo.

14:10.217 --> 14:12.611
Doctor, please say a few words.

14:12.942 --> 14:13.847
But...

14:14.194 --> 14:16.076
Don't be so bashful.

14:16.529 --> 14:17.738
OK.

14:23.077 --> 14:25.078
I am Shimizu from the clinic.

14:25.747 --> 14:27.677
This is a very nice auditorium.

14:27.999 --> 14:33.587
But wasn't there something else we should
have done before building a new auditorium?

14:33.588 --> 14:37.674
I believe we should have reinforced
the cliff behind the school instead.

14:39.117 --> 14:43.931
With this torrential rain, the soil might be loosening
and there could be another disaster soon.

14:44.437 --> 14:47.678
We could have more victims like my brother.

14:48.561 --> 14:51.438
People of this village and our esteemed officials,

14:52.357 --> 14:56.151
I ask you to work on the cliff, not this auditorium!

15:12.085 --> 15:13.168
What's the matter?

15:28.601 --> 15:33.313
<i>Why do I feel so calm when I'm with him?</i>

15:34.983 --> 15:38.781
<i>Why can I cry so openly around him?</i>

15:40.238 --> 15:44.060
<i>I haven't felt so relaxed since I lost my brother.</i>

15:44.450 --> 15:45.253
<i>It's...</i>

15:45.952 --> 15:48.131
<i>Right, it's...</i>

15:52.542 --> 15:55.085
Why haven't you gotten married?

15:55.586 --> 15:57.182
I'm just a hooligan.

15:58.464 --> 16:00.590
I am the stink of the medical professionals.

16:00.591 --> 16:02.622
I can't possibly marry.

16:03.219 --> 16:05.554
But you perform such wonderful surgeries.

16:05.779 --> 16:07.643
You're even more wonderful.

16:08.266 --> 16:10.600
You're working so hard tending to the kids, all by yourself.

16:11.894 --> 16:14.302
It doesn't matter how skilled you
are or what your specialty is.

16:14.731 --> 16:16.796
What's amazing is how you can keep up with it all.

16:17.024 --> 16:17.816
But...

16:18.901 --> 16:21.278
I'm thinking about leaving this island.

16:22.447 --> 16:23.100
Why?

16:24.907 --> 16:28.368
Because you're leaving.

16:31.706 --> 16:32.492
Absurd.

16:32.832 --> 16:33.832
That's stupid.

16:33.833 --> 16:36.369
No, it's not stupid.

16:36.919 --> 16:37.956
I'm serious.

16:38.463 --> 16:41.044
Forget about me.

16:42.049 --> 16:45.552
I guess I'm just distracting you.

16:47.180 --> 16:48.346
No.

16:48.735 --> 16:49.639
No.

16:50.224 --> 16:51.141
No!

16:52.101 --> 16:53.768
No...

17:08.618 --> 17:09.417
<i>Absurd.</i>

17:09.785 --> 17:10.938
<i>That's stupid.</i>

17:11.621 --> 17:14.498
<i>I guess I'm just distracting you.</i>

17:15.249 --> 17:17.292
<i>Forget about me.</i>

17:23.466 --> 17:24.716
Not there.

17:25.134 --> 17:27.719
It's dangerous under that cliff!

17:28.262 --> 17:29.554
They can't hear me.

17:30.640 --> 17:32.599
Move away from there!

17:42.401 --> 17:43.360
What?!

17:46.197 --> 17:49.241
People with type O and type A blood,
give your blood for these two!

17:51.744 --> 17:56.164
If they die while the principal is on
medical leave, it will be my responsibility.

17:56.165 --> 17:59.668
Doctor, please save her!

18:00.211 --> 18:01.849
Move out of my way.

18:02.630 --> 18:05.173
Are you going to work on both of them at the same time?

18:05.174 --> 18:06.716
Can you really do it?

18:06.717 --> 18:07.926
That's hard to believe.

18:18.646 --> 18:19.980
I'm in awe.

18:19.981 --> 18:23.233
His hands are moving like a machine.

18:24.396 --> 18:27.915
Mr. Mayor, both of them have five internal ruptures each.

18:28.239 --> 18:30.372
Will the village pay the fee for the surgeries?

18:30.892 --> 18:32.158
It'll be ¥ 100,000,000.

18:34.370 --> 18:36.496
We don't have that kind of money...

18:37.123 --> 18:39.916
You still have the money you were going to use to pay the
construction company for the auditorium, don't you?

18:39.917 --> 18:41.918
But that's...

18:42.294 --> 18:44.462
You should ask them to wait.

18:45.156 --> 18:47.900
You didn't have the money to fix a cliff
that posed an eminent danger,

18:48.259 --> 18:50.885
but you couldn't wait to pay for an auditorium?

19:01.188 --> 19:03.679
<i>Her coronary arteries are
underdeveloped, they're too small.</i>

19:04.150 --> 19:05.964
<i>She cannot withstand an operation.</i>

19:06.444 --> 19:09.842
<i>But with five internal ruptures,
she can't be saved without one.</i>

19:10.489 --> 19:12.540
<i>I just need to complete this fast.</i>

19:12.950 --> 19:15.729
<i>Damn it! I won't let them die like this!</i>

19:18.581 --> 19:20.039
The operations are complete.

19:20.040 --> 19:21.032
Now, go home.

19:21.959 --> 19:24.711
Will they live?

19:31.218 --> 19:32.052
I can't tell.

19:33.220 --> 19:34.515
But I'm isolating the patients!

19:34.764 --> 19:35.470
So leave!

19:35.723 --> 19:36.806
Black...

19:37.975 --> 19:40.143
Dr. Black Jack,

19:41.812 --> 19:43.820
will the girl live?

19:44.190 --> 19:46.107
Yes, she will.

19:46.942 --> 19:48.092
Good.

19:48.402 --> 19:50.153
Thank you, Doctor.

19:52.656 --> 19:53.821
Doctor,

19:54.033 --> 19:54.949
What is it?

19:56.452 --> 20:01.414
when I saw the kid getting swallowed by
the mudslide, I wanted to save her.

20:02.792 --> 20:05.670
I thought that was my duty.

20:06.545 --> 20:08.836
Yes, that's right.

20:09.256 --> 20:11.049
But don't talk anymore.

20:11.050 --> 20:12.383
You're overtaxing your heart.

20:13.093 --> 20:16.155
But I won't make it, will I?

20:16.347 --> 20:17.514
What are you saying?!

20:18.557 --> 20:23.019
I wanted to live a little longer on this ilsland.

20:23.020 --> 20:23.729
Stop that!

20:23.986 --> 20:24.900
Cheer up!

20:25.147 --> 20:26.356
And live!

20:26.357 --> 20:27.482
You still have hope!

20:29.151 --> 20:30.360
Doctor,

20:32.988 --> 20:35.657
can I have the scalpel?

20:35.658 --> 20:36.533
The scalpel?

20:37.284 --> 20:40.248
Your wonderful scalpel.

20:44.166 --> 20:45.333
Thank you.

20:47.086 --> 20:50.880
Now I have no regrets before I die.

20:51.382 --> 20:55.052
Kiyomi-san, don't say that!

20:58.973 --> 21:02.684
You finally called me by my name.

21:20.160 --> 21:22.036
Dr. Shimizu,

21:22.621 --> 21:24.956
are you awake?

21:24.957 --> 21:27.268
You've been healed!

21:27.543 --> 21:29.652
And the girl as well.

